      "independent_reference": {
        "source": "Linear semi-Lagrangian advection-operator gradient: for a constant velocity the bilinear backtrace map is the exact sparse linear operator M (advect(u0)=M u0), so for the K-step rollout dLoss/du0 = 2 (M^K)^T (M^K u0 - target), EXACT. The NumPy advect mirror replicates the reference _sl_advect_2d_k op-order so M is bit-faithful to the Warp engine (CPU f64); autodiff matches the analytic operator to ~4e-15. Hand-derived; semi-Lagrangian backtrace per Stam, J. (1999), 'Stable Fluids', SIGGRAPH '99, 121-128 (DOI 10.1145/311535.311548).",
        "derived_by": "closed-form-analytic (linear-advection operator)",
