      "independent_reference": {
        "source": "Discrete-diffusion analytic: one explicit step u' = u0 + dt*nu*Lap(u0) is exactly linear in nu, so dLoss/dnu = 2 (u' - target) . (dt * Lap(u0)), closed-form. Distinct from A1/A2 in physical term (diffusion, not advection), parameter (the coefficient nu, not the field u0), and method (heat-operator linearization, not the advection adjoint). Hand-derived; the heat equation d_t u = nu Lap(u) is the physical source. autodiff == analytic EXACT (0.0).",
